WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.386 --> 00:00:01.534
- Rent a brain.

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.505
We may be tokens, but we're
damn good-looking ones.

00:00:03.505 --> 00:00:05.883
You think it would
dishonor Dr. King's memory

00:00:05.883 --> 00:00:07.949
if I went to sit in the back of the bus?

00:00:07.949 --> 00:00:11.541
- So we need to talk about
how iconic Jodie Landon is.

00:00:11.541 --> 00:00:14.124
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.196 --> 00:00:19.863
20 years ago, Daria came to MTV.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:23.257
The show focused on
the shade icon herself,

00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:25.952
Daria Morgendorffer and
her family and schoolmates

00:00:25.952 --> 00:00:27.242
and Lawndale High.

00:00:27.242 --> 00:00:28.557
- This looks well-balanced.

00:00:28.557 --> 00:00:29.605
- Ew.
- Dammit,

00:00:29.605 --> 00:00:31.586
we've got four mouths to feed!

00:00:31.586 --> 00:00:33.526
Food costs money.
- I knew it.

00:00:33.526 --> 00:00:35.638
- The show was really ahead of its time

00:00:35.638 --> 00:00:38.996
It touched on feminism, social
class, and thanks to one

00:00:38.996 --> 00:00:42.538
of the show's few characters
of color, Jodie, race as well.

00:00:42.538 --> 00:00:45.769
Homegirl literally ran
Lawndale High School.

00:00:45.769 --> 00:00:48.105
- Thank you, Jodie Landon,
Valedictorian of her graduating

00:00:48.105 --> 00:00:50.309
class of Lawndale High.

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:51.881
- I'm president of the French club,

00:00:51.881 --> 00:00:54.640
Vice President of Student
Council, editor of yearbook,

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.418
and I'm also on the tennis team.

00:00:56.418 --> 00:00:59.294
- She had the black
boyfriend, box braids popping,

00:00:59.294 --> 00:01:02.575
unapologetic attitude, she
carried herself with so much

00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:03.712
class and dignity.

00:01:03.712 --> 00:01:05.164
- Someday I'd like to own my own business,

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:08.500
maybe a consulting firm geared
toward minority startups.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.480
- She truly was someone that I wanted

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:11.695
to be best friends with.

00:01:11.695 --> 00:01:14.534
But she was also very
vocal about what it mean

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:17.852
to be under this gaze of
being the perfect minority

00:01:17.852 --> 00:01:19.338
and the token black girl.

00:01:19.338 --> 00:01:22.549
- At home, I'm Jodie, I can
say or do whatever feels right,

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:25.543
but at school, I'm the
Queen of the Negroes,

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:28.960
the perfect African-American
teen, the role model

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.787
for all of the other
African-American teens at Lawndale,

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:33.755
oops, where'd they do?

00:01:33.755 --> 00:01:36.694
- To its credit, the show
positioned Jodie to be the biggest

00:01:36.694 --> 00:01:39.136
critic of the show's
overwhelming whiteness.

00:01:39.136 --> 00:01:41.023
- Isn't it great how they keep electing us

00:01:41.023 --> 00:01:43.301
Homecoming King and Queen every year?

00:01:43.301 --> 00:01:45.760
- Yes, it's such a generous
and enlightened gesture,

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.991
it completely makes up
for the town's utter lack

00:01:47.991 --> 00:01:49.541
of diversity in my mind.

00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:52.140
- And we're playing into it.
- Damn college application.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.653
- This is so humiliating.

00:01:53.653 --> 00:01:56.695
- Jodie was woke before woke
even knew what woke was.

00:01:56.695 --> 00:01:58.001
- Why play into this stupid charade

00:01:58.001 --> 00:02:00.084
any more than we have to?

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.421
- What happened?
- Oh what the hell,

00:02:06.421 --> 00:02:09.464
we may be tokens but we're
damn good-looking ones.

00:02:09.464 --> 00:02:12.100
- Not only were Jodie and
her boyfriend Mack Mackenzie

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.388
some of the few characters of color,

00:02:14.388 --> 00:02:17.673
but they were also the
only secondary characters

00:02:17.673 --> 00:02:19.891
to have a three-dimensional storyline

00:02:19.891 --> 00:02:21.908
independent from the show's white lead.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.028
In the show's film-length
finale Is It College Yet?

00:02:25.028 --> 00:02:27.206
Jodie and her parents
debate over which college

00:02:27.206 --> 00:02:28.884
Jodie was going to go to.

00:02:28.884 --> 00:02:31.211
Would it be the elitest Ivy
League school Questmoore

00:02:31.211 --> 00:02:33.733
or the historically black college Turner.

00:02:33.733 --> 00:02:36.077
- I wanna go to Turner, at
least for a year or two.

00:02:36.077 --> 00:02:37.523
- You wanna go to college to relax?

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:40.005
- Relax socially, stop being the black kid

00:02:40.005 --> 00:02:42.679
and just be a kid, I'm tired
of being in the extreme

00:02:42.679 --> 00:02:44.818
minority and I don't wanna
go to a place where people

00:02:44.818 --> 00:02:47.951
might think I got in just
because I'm African-American.

00:02:47.951 --> 00:02:50.533
- Now in the end, Jodie
chooses to go to Turner

00:02:50.533 --> 00:02:52.117
with her parents' support.

00:02:52.117 --> 00:02:54.163
- My parents said if I was
so upset about Questmoore

00:02:54.163 --> 00:02:56.296
that I'd apply to Turner
behind their backs,

00:02:56.296 --> 00:02:58.624
they had to respect my feelings,
they told me I'd earned

00:02:58.624 --> 00:03:00.524
the right to be treated like an adult.

00:03:00.524 --> 00:03:03.293
- As we look back on the
20-year anniversary of Daria,

00:03:03.293 --> 00:03:04.973
it's time that we give Jodie Landon

00:03:04.973 --> 00:03:07.529
the respect and credit that she deserves.

00:03:07.529 --> 00:03:10.104
Her poise and dignity to
personify what it means

00:03:10.104 --> 00:03:12.021
to be black girl magic.

